WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.102
Every proposal, contract and service agreement now
has a Ready to send

00:00:04.102 --> 00:00:06.603
check at the top of its Review step.

00:00:06.603 --> 00:00:10.979
This training document has two things wrong with it:
a line with no price,

00:00:10.979 --> 00:00:13.480
and a placeholder that was never filled in.

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:17.232
Each one says what the client would actually see on
the page,

00:00:17.232 --> 00:00:19.733
and the preview beside it shows exactly that.

00:00:20.833 --> 00:00:24.933
Every line has a button that takes you to the field
that fixes it.

00:00:24.933 --> 00:00:28.154
This one lands on the table row with the empty
amount.

00:00:28.154 --> 00:00:31.668
Type the price, come back to Review, and that line
is gone.

00:00:31.668 --> 00:00:34.889
The check runs against the document as it stands on
screen,

00:00:34.889 --> 00:00:37.525
so you see the result before anything is saved.

00:00:38.625 --> 00:00:42.730
It also reads what a contract says against who it is
for.

00:00:42.730 --> 00:00:46.151
This service contract names Maryland in its sales
tax clause,

00:00:46.151 --> 00:00:48.203
and the client is in Oregon.

00:00:48.203 --> 00:00:52.992
Set the state in the contract details, and the
document reads ready to send.

00:00:54.092 --> 00:00:56.258
Underneath it is What changed.

00:00:56.258 --> 00:01:00.589
It compares the document with the version the client
received.

00:01:00.589 --> 00:01:05.787
Exporting the PDF records that version, so straight
after an export it

00:01:05.787 --> 00:01:07.519
reads: nothing has changed.

00:01:08.619 --> 00:01:09.983
Now change a price.

00:01:09.983 --> 00:01:14.074
What changed lists it under Price: the line that
moved, the table

00:01:14.074 --> 00:01:18.165
it sits in and the document total, each with what it
was,

00:01:18.165 --> 00:01:22.255
what it is now, and the difference, and the summary
carries the

00:01:22.255 --> 00:01:23.619
move in the total.

00:01:23.619 --> 00:01:27.710
Scope, quantities, price, margin and terms are read
the same way, in

00:01:27.710 --> 00:01:29.073
that order, every time.

00:01:30.173 --> 00:01:33.614
Every export and share link becomes a version you
can compare against.

00:01:33.614 --> 00:01:37.055
If the one you emailed was not the latest, pick it
here

00:01:37.055 --> 00:01:39.636
and mark it as the one the client received.

00:01:39.636 --> 00:01:42.503
The comparison then defaults to it until you say
otherwise.
